@MugaSofer @anthrupad Two clarifications here:
- I think writing down plans doesn't get you very far, the best plans are often things like "try X, see what happens, iterate".
- It's about beating any human (across many domains) not beating the best human in each domain.

@TonyZador @BAPearlmutter I think the miscommunication here is that, within the field, the "skynet" and "paperclip" scenarios are seen as roughly equivalent. Both involve:
- an AI which wants to achieve something against human interests
- and which takes over the world in order to achieve it...
